Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.85,0:00:08.84,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,Cyclops to Handler One.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.84,0:00:12.93,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,They've reached the old high-speed \Nrailroad terminal at point 122.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.18,0:00:17.33,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,Sorry. They were jamming the radar, \Nand it took us a while to find them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.59,0:00:20.55,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,This is gonna be a rough fight \Nfor the new kids.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.96,0:00:23.08,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,What do we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.29,0:00:25.34,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Deploy our main force at 062,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.34,0:00:27.28,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,then lure them in with another unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.28,0:00:30.29,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,That would put them in range \Nof the remaining howitzers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.62,0:00:33.10,Italics,Shiden,0,0,0,,So we're fighting them \Nright in front of the base, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.34,0:00:35.50,Italics,Shiden,0,0,0,,If they make it through, \Nthere's nothing but the minefields
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.50,0:00:37.04,Italics,Shiden,0,0,0,,and the howitzers \Nto keep them out, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.78,0:00:42.68,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,But it's the best location we have, \Nif we're to survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.29,0:00:47.28,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,Yes, my Queen!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.93,0:00:56.78,Italics Top,News,0,0,0,,Now for today's update on the war \Nfrom San Magnolia Military HQ!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.14,0:01:01.85,Italics Top,News,0,0,0,,Our nation's autonomous Juggernaut units \Nintercepted the Legion mechanized infantry drones,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.74,0:01:01.74,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,{\fad(486,473)}December 2nd, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.85,0:01:05.71,Italics Top,News,0,0,0,,dealt critical damage, \Nand forced them to withdraw.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.71,0:01:08.99,Italics,News,0,0,0,,Combat via highly advanced, \Nethically responsible drones
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.99,0:01:12.05,Italics,News,0,0,0,,has resulted in zero fatalities \Non our side!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.68,0:01:18.47,Italics,News,0,0,0,,The day when our righteous nation finally smashes \Nthe evil remnants of the wicked Empire is not far off!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.80,0:01:22.88,Italics,News,0,0,0,,Glory to the Republic of San Magnolia, \Nand to the five-color flag!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.48,0:01:30.37,Main,Man 1,0,0,0,,Hey, it's the Doll-Crushing Princess!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.37,0:01:33.29,Main,Man 1,0,0,0,,I heard you had another victory \Nagainst the Legion threat today,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.29,0:01:35.14,Main,Man 1,0,0,0,,stained with the blood of pigs!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.14,0:01:39.69,Main,Man 2,0,0,0,,That's why they call her Bloody Regina, \Nthe bloody queen!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.92,0:01:44.09,Main,Man 1,0,0,0,,You learn to tell the difference \Nbetween men and pigs?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.24,0:01:46.91,Main,Man 2,0,0,0,,She never changes expression.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.91,0:01:48.96,Main,Man 2,0,0,0,,Who knows what she's thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.96,0:01:51.65,Main,Man 3,0,0,0,,Getting demoted for the sake of those pigs...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.65,0:01:54.10,Main,Man 3,0,0,0,,Wearing a black uniform \Nwhen nobody else does...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.34,0:01:58.67,Main,Man 1,0,0,0,,The Legion won't even be around \Nin two years!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.67,0:02:00.67,Main,Man 2,0,0,0,,Her family's rich and famous, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.67,0:02:04.02,Main,Man 2,0,0,0,,Had she just done nothing, \Nshe'd have life on easy street.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.06,0:02:10.11,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.43,0:02:11.38,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,Morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.87,0:02:15.47,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,There's something I want to check up\N on from what you asked.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.47,0:02:17.62,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,The additional settings \Non the RAID Device.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.94,0:02:18.99,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.29,0:02:21.10,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I'll be there in two hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.10,0:02:22.68,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,Okay, see you then.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.02,0:02:31.95,Main,Lieutenant Colonel,0,0,0,,How many times do I have to tell you, \N"Captain" Milizé?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.39,0:02:38.46,Main,Lieutenant Colonel,0,0,0,,Unauthorized use of the howitzers. \NUnscheduled supply drops.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.46,0:02:40.83,Main,Lieutenant Colonel,0,0,0,,Taking direct command \Nof units not below you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.39,0:02:44.18,Main,Lieutenant Colonel,0,0,0,,Do you know how many\N complaints I'm getting?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.50,0:02:48.81,Main,Lieutenant Colonel,0,0,0,,Don't make me do extra work \Nfor the sake of the damn Eighty-Six.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.81,0:02:51.78,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,If you'd give me permission in advance,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.78,0:02:54.50,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,you wouldn't have to tell me any of this, \NLieutenant Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.82,0:02:55.99,Main,Lieutenant Colonel,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.99,0:02:59.90,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,You, and all of them, are free \Nto complain all you like,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.90,0:03:02.22,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,but it has nothing to do with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.22,0:03:03.94,Main,Lieutenant Colonel,0,0,0,,You little brat!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.28,0:03:06.52,Main,Lieutenant Colonel,0,0,0,,Know your place! \NYou're just a captain!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.52,0:03:08.46,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Are you sure you want me \Nto know my place?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.16,0:03:12.84,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Your subordinates' results reflect \Non your own career.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.84,0:03:14.22,Main,Lieutenant Colonel,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.22,0:03:15.96,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I'm currently the top Handler.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.96,0:03:21.72,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,If my Legion kill rate goes down, \Nyou risk not being promoted.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.24,0:03:23.12,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.76,0:03:32.42,Main,Lieutenant Colonel,0,0,0,,Watch your mouth, Captain.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.42,0:03:35.03,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Excuse me, Lieutenant Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.18,0:04:10.66,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I'll let you handle the supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.66,0:04:11.33,Main,Woman,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.63,0:04:13.62,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,Captain, I looked into \Nhow many of the howitzers
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.62,0:04:17.18,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,in the rear of Southern Combat District 8 \Nwere still functional, and you were right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.18,0:04:19.91,Main,Officer,0,0,0,,It was around twenty percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.91,0:04:21.60,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I thought so.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.18,0:04:23.80,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Our total attrition rate \Non the front lines—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.80,0:04:28.05,Main,Girls,0,0,0,,Hey, look! Look! Snow!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.53,0:04:33.60,Main,Woman,0,0,0,,Winter's really here, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.28,0:04:38.00,Italics,Shiden,0,0,0,,Cyclops to Handler One.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.00,0:04:39.01,Italics,Shiden,0,0,0,,Do you read?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.33,0:04:41.34,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Yes. What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.34,0:04:43.83,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,We found an enemy unit \Nout on patrol.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.05,0:04:45.33,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,We need your orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.52,0:04:46.70,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.31,0:04:49.03,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Keep it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.60,0:04:52.93,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Cyclops, give me a report.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.49,0:05:02.21,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Sorry I'm late.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.46,0:05:06.58,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,You're pretty early.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.68,0:05:15.11,Main,Annette,0,0,0,,Get started with your chat.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.96,0:05:18.77,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.90,0:05:27.24,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Understood. Thank you for the report.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.24,0:05:31.78,Italics,Shiden,0,0,0,,Yeah. I'll be waiting for those \NLegion force estimates, Queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.78,0:05:33.92,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Yes, I'll do what I can.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.59,0:05:38.69,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,Let's both work together \Nto do our best.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.15,0:05:41.88,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.88,0:05:46.44,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,You're our Handler. \NWe're counting on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.67,0:05:47.85,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,You, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.85,0:05:51.90,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,I need the info you give us \Nfrom the battlefield, Cyclops.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.55,0:05:57.69,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,It's okay to call me \Nby my real name now, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.97,0:05:58.85,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,If you aren't going to,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.83,0:06:01.34,sign_8604_94_Shiden_Iida,Onscreen,0,0,0,,Shiden Iida
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.85,0:06:01.11,Italics,Shiden,0,0,0,,why did you ask?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.58,0:06:03.76,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,Because that's...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.79,0:06:10.56,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,my responsibility as a Handler.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.23,0:06:15.87,Italics,Shiden,0,0,0,,You're always so serious \Nand formal, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.54,0:06:19.77,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,Think what you like.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.60,0:06:26.31,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,Thanks to you, though, \Nwe might live a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.75,0:06:30.28,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,I appreciate it, but we might be going \Nto Spearhead in a few months.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.03,0:06:37.15,Italics,Shiden,0,0,0,,The strongest guy I know finally got sent \Non Special Recon a while back.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.72,0:06:40.49,Italics,Shiden,0,0,0,,He's probably dead now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.80,0:06:45.26,Italics,Shiden,0,0,0,,The headless Reaper who always used blades.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.15,0:06:54.47,Italics,Shiden,0,0,0,,Which do you think will be first: \Nus going there or the Legion coming here?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.33,0:06:56.49,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.96,0:07:04.70,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,But my job now is to prepare for the\N large-scale Legion offensive I think is coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.71,0:07:09.27,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,I've already decided to help you, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.27,0:07:11.31,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,no preparations you make \Nwill change a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.84,0:07:13.21,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,You're doing it anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.74,0:07:18.89,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,I'm doing it anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.96,0:07:26.71,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,But Cyclops, don't forget \Nyour reports on patrol.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.13,0:07:28.40,Main,Shiden,0,0,0,,Roger!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.44,0:07:39.86,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,They told me to survive, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.21,0:07:45.80,Main,Lena,0,0,0,,They believed in me, \Nand told me to fight, and survive.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.28,0:07:52.53,sign_11276_115_Teppy,Onscreen,0,0,0,,Teppy
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.67,0:07:58.83,Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,To live up to the hopes of those \Nwho are no longer with us...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.52,0:08:07.37,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,Shin!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.90,0:08:29.55,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,This is as far as I can go.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.93,0:08:33.78,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,You can go the rest \Nof the way yourself, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.37,0:08:36.46,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,You've got your comrades going with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.98,0:08:44.41,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,You've really grown up, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.85,0:08:49.38,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,Don't let me keep you a prisoner.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.09,0:08:52.71,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,You can forget about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.96,0:08:58.76,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.59,0:09:03.34,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,I want you to remember me, \Njust once in a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.49,0:09:08.57,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,Live free, be happy...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.90,0:09:11.69,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,And once in a while, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.67,0:09:13.90,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,Just once in a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.61,0:09:17.78,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,Be well.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.16,0:09:22.67,Main,Rei,0,0,0,,And please be happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.31,0:09:33.48,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.19,0:10:11.91,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I know. \NI just want to chat a little.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.64,0:10:18.05,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,You're awake, huh? Hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.84,0:10:22.04,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Will you tell me your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.24,0:10:26.02,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.23,0:10:32.01,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Oh, the generals were all really worried, \Nso they made me wear this biohazard suit.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.48,0:10:35.02,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,But it's rude to be wearing this, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.43,0:10:40.89,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,My name is Ernst.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.89,0:10:42.03,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,And you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.32,0:10:47.40,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Shin Nouzen.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.47,0:10:52.36,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Welcome to the Federacy of Giad!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.08,0:10:54.02,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,"Giad"?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.02,0:10:56.41,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Oh, I should explain.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.41,0:11:02.33,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,We defeated the Giad "Empire" that created the Legion, \Nand we changed it into a Federal Republic.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.33,0:11:06.64,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Well, because of that, we're still \Nfighting the remaining Legion, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.98,0:11:13.30,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,We found you captured by the Legion \Non the western front of the war.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.84,0:11:18.37,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Sorry, sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.37,0:11:20.54,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Of course you're worried.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.77,0:11:28.62,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,You were sleeping, \Nso we turned the windows opaque.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.37,0:11:37.83,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Neither you nor we entirely\N understand what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.18,0:11:40.46,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Later, when you remember, \Nif you could...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.46,0:11:42.55,Italics,Nurse,0,0,0,,Sir! That's enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.71,0:11:44.59,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.04,0:11:48.60,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,The scary lady's going to get mad at me, \Nso I'll be going.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.95,0:11:50.48,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,But remember this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.83,0:11:56.22,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,You're the first foreign visitors we've had \Nsince our nation's founding.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.22,0:12:01.66,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,We were too busy with the Legion \Nto put together customs procedures.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.66,0:12:04.10,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,But don't worry, we will not harm you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.14,0:12:08.74,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I'm Ernst Zimerman,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.32,0:12:13.62,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,provisional President of the Giad Federacy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.89,0:12:16.12,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,What does our analysis show?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.44,0:12:22.51,Main,Analyst,0,0,0,,It's safe to say they aren't agents \Nof San Magnolia or any other country.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.72,0:12:24.62,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,And the odds that \Nthey're a new type of Legion,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.62,0:12:28.38,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,or perhaps a carrier\N for a Legion bioweapon?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.38,0:12:32.94,Main,Analyst,0,0,0,,Our tests and the scan we did after they\N were brought in show nothing irregular.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.94,0:12:34.52,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,And the things they had with them?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.78,0:12:38.89,Main,Analyst,0,0,0,,It's a slightly older model, \Nbut definitely a Dinosauria.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.43,0:12:42.53,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,And the things on their ears?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.93,0:12:46.03,Main,Analyst,0,0,0,,A communication device, as they said.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.32,0:12:50.98,Main,Analyst,0,0,0,,It artificially recreates the mental links \Nthat a certain family is capable of.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.98,0:12:52.17,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Revolutionary.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.74,0:12:57.61,Main,Giad Officer,0,0,0,,The safest thing for the Federacy \Nwould be to eliminate them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.59,0:13:05.39,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,Shin,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.29,0:13:08.80,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,you were out for three whole days.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.80,0:13:12.60,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,Seriously, Kurena was bawling her eyes out.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.60,0:13:13.69,Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,I was not!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.69,0:13:20.56,Italics,Anju,0,0,0,,Shin, I know now's not a good time,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.56,0:13:24.19,Italics,Anju,0,0,0,,but be ready when you get better.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.70,0:13:28.37,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,Sorry, we all feel the same way.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.37,0:13:31.71,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,If you ever pull that shit again, \NI will kick your ass.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.71,0:13:35.21,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I didn't mean to die—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.21,0:13:36.41,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,You're going to make me mad.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.41,0:13:41.17,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,Even if you didn't intend to die, \Nyou knew you would if you fought alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.81,0:13:45.07,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,We've all thought about it once, sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.07,0:13:46.93,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,But that's why we can't forgive it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.33,0:13:50.09,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,Because we understand! \NIt's cheating.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.08,0:13:52.85,Italics,Theo,0,0,0,,Never do that again!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.52,0:13:55.80,Italics,Kurena,0,0,0,,I was so worried!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.72,0:14:01.89,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.83,0:14:09.41,Italics,Raiden,0,0,0,,But who knows what happens now...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.95,0:14:18.16,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,So yeah, from now on, \Nyou're citizens of the Federacy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.17,0:14:22.04,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.46,0:14:28.19,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,We haven't seen you for a month, \Nand the first thing you say is "So yeah?"
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.19,0:14:29.34,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.34,0:14:32.13,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,You sure you want \Nto make a bunch of strange kids
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.13,0:14:34.42,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,who were kicked out \Nof their old country into citizens?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.18,0:14:38.38,Main,Theo,0,0,0,,Wouldn't it be safer just to kill us?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.38,0:14:40.15,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,Is that what you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.28,0:14:44.52,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,What benefit do you get \Nfrom saving us?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.52,0:14:49.75,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,A society which refuses to save children \Nbecause there's no "benefit"
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.75,0:14:52.16,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,is a society which in the end \Nbenefits no one.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.53,0:14:58.79,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,And if humanity can't survive except\N by killing children because they're "strange,"
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.05,0:15:03.31,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,humanity would be better off dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.23,0:15:12.02,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,Anyway, I'll be your guardian \Nfor a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.72,0:15:15.58,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,So rest a bit, see this country,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.14,0:15:19.73,Italics,Ernst,0,0,0,,and then think about what you'll do.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.69,0:15:27.69,sign_22147_207_Sankt_Glykine_Ba,Onscreen,0,0,0,,Sankt Glykine Base
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.98,0:15:31.42,Main Top,Richard,0,0,0,,Those war machines we recovered\N—the "Juggernauts"?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.19,0:15:31.70,Dates,Onscreen,0,0,0,,{\fad(486,473)}December 2nd, Stellar Year 2148
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.42,0:15:35.61,Main Top,Richard,0,0,0,,Their capabilities aside, \Nwhat was done with them is amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.61,0:15:37.46,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,I'd love to hear more.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.46,0:15:41.17,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,Hey, I'm first. \NWe won't let you have them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.17,0:15:42.01,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.01,0:15:46.10,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,High-mobility combat data and people \Nwith actual combat experience against the data.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.10,0:15:48.76,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,They're perfect as operators \Nfor my prototypes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.09,0:15:51.62,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,They'd be wasted on those slow Vánagandr.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.62,0:15:53.14,Main,Richard,0,0,0,,What did you say, spider woman?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.14,0:15:54.46,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,What did you say, beetle?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.46,0:15:57.57,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,You're all free to talk to them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.57,0:15:59.81,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,But I won't let them be operators.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.81,0:16:02.17,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,We'd be no different from the Republic.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.17,0:16:04.60,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,But they're all saying in \Ntheir counseling sessions
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.60,0:16:07.48,Main,Grethe,0,0,0,,that they want to go back \Nto the battlefield.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.86,0:16:14.04,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,That's because the battlefield\N is all they know right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.77,0:16:17.36,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Actions should be met with rewards.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.61,0:16:21.99,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,If they've fought for so long, \Nthey should be given peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.57,0:16:25.99,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Especially if their homeland \Nrefuses to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.01,0:16:30.68,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I want the Federacy to be just, at least.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.15,0:16:32.01,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Because...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.41,0:16:36.35,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,that is the ideal of mankind.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.57,0:17:05.91,Main,Citizen 1,0,0,0,,Let us save our pitiful comrades!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.91,0:17:07.69,Main,Citizens,0,0,0,,Let's save them!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.69,0:17:10.69,Main,Citizen 1,0,0,0,,The Eighty-Six are victims!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.69,0:17:12.32,Main,Citizens,0,0,0,,Victims!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.32,0:17:15.19,Main,Citizen 1,0,0,0,,Let us save our pitiful comrades!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.18,0:17:20.06,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,They were all happy when you were saved,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.19,0:17:16.82,Main Top,Citizens,0,0,0,,Let's save them!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.06,0:17:24.32,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,because they learned there was \Na surviving country besides our own.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.72,0:17:27.96,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,But when they learned \Nhow you were treated,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.96,0:17:32.31,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,they became overcome with the desire \Nto save you and your comrades.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.00,0:17:42.62,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,This is my house, \Nbut from now on it's your home.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.09,0:17:47.61,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Welcome!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.60,0:17:48.27,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.27,0:17:49.92,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Push that desk!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.92,0:17:51.56,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,We need to hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.83,0:17:59.05,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Welcome, poor souls who were banished \Nfrom your country!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.42,0:18:07.30,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Great Giad welcomes you \Nwith pity and compassion!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.30,0:18:10.37,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,We don't expect any kind of recompense \Nfrom low-borns like you,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.37,0:18:13.16,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,so your thanks are enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.09,0:18:15.80,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Hey, red-eyes!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.80,0:18:17.95,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Why are you looking away?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.95,0:18:19.41,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,I thought there might be someone else here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.41,0:18:21.87,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,You shut the door!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.87,0:18:23.33,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Are you making fun of me?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.33,0:18:23.93,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.14,0:18:28.31,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,This is the problem with low-born people \Nfrom the Republic.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.31,0:18:29.31,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,Is this your daughter?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.31,0:18:32.91,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,I hate to say it, but you need \Nto discipline her better.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.91,0:18:36.41,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Oh, no. \NShe's not my daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.72,0:18:39.11,Main Top,Frederica,0,0,0,,Do you really think I'm the daughter \Nof this lowly bureaucrat?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.11,0:18:40.12,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I'm—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.63,0:18:41.68,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Frederica Rosenfort.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.90,0:18:44.88,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Some things happened, \Nand now she's staying here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.90,0:18:51.53,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,It's annoying to explain to everyone,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.77,0:18:54.81,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,so I've got her down on \Npaper as my daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.81,0:18:59.01,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,But regardless, \Nyou'll be living together for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.01,0:19:04.26,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,So I'd appreciate it if you'd think of her \Nas a slightly naïve little sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.77,0:19:07.27,Main,Raiden,0,0,0,,"Little sister," huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.27,0:19:12.08,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Oh, on paper, I've adopted you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.08,0:19:15.07,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,So you can call me "Dad," \Nif you want.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.81,0:19:23.22,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I'm joking.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.50,0:19:31.68,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,What's that on your neck?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.96,0:19:34.08,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Frederica, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.44,0:19:36.44,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I told you their situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.87,0:19:40.44,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,You have wounds \Nyou don't want touched, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.54,0:19:49.71,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I'm the cute little sister \Nyou've been given to heal your wounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.08,0:19:53.86,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,The family and home \Nand happiness you lost...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.86,0:19:58.03,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,The noble and compassionate \NFederacy is willing to give you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.33,0:20:01.09,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Be very nice to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.55,0:20:02.55,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Big brothers and sisters!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.78,0:20:09.82,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Theresa, they're being mean!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.82,0:20:10.98,Main,Theresa,0,0,0,,Right, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.98,0:20:15.67,Main,Theresa,0,0,0,,Frederica, everything that just happened \Nwas your own fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.02,0:20:18.96,Main Top,Frederica,0,0,0,,Was not! Was not!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.56,0:20:21.73,Main,Theresa,0,0,0,,I'm Theresa. \NI'll be taking care of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.06,0:20:26.96,Main,Theresa,0,0,0,,Welcome home, everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.71,0:20:34.44,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,I'm bored. \NThey all went to sleep so early.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.10,0:20:43.36,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Sorry, I know you're tired.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.79,0:20:45.62,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I was holding on to this.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.94,0:20:47.69,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,It was in your war machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.70,0:20:49.83,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Is it yours?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.80,0:20:55.69,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.29,0:21:01.61,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Thank you, Theresa.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.61,0:21:03.39,Main,Theresa,0,0,0,,Not at all, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.39,0:21:08.08,Main,Theresa,0,0,0,,Kids that age eat a lot. \NIt's fun to cook for them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.35,0:21:12.05,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,I'm sorry. \NThis is likely to be difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.32,0:21:18.54,Main,Theresa,0,0,0,,Not at all. \NServing you is my job.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.76,0:21:25.79,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Do you think it's a stupid way \Nof trying to compensate for things?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.67,0:21:29.75,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,That I'm using them \Nas a replacement?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.75,0:21:33.54,Main,Theresa,0,0,0,,No. They could never be that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.54,0:21:39.44,Main,Theresa,0,0,0,,Every person is their own, \Nirreplaceable individual.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.44,0:21:43.38,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,But still, people try to bury the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.38,0:21:45.79,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,In whatever way they can.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.14,0:21:48.32,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Whom are you talking to,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.97,0:21:50.29,Main,Ernst,0,0,0,,Empress?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.77,0:21:59.71,Main,Frederica,0,0,0,,Kiri...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.18,0:23:38.69,Main,Shin,0,0,0,,"It's Too Late."
